  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member of a group MP, I want to see who takes part in the conversation once I open it, so that I know who reads it, without crowding the Messages list with a list that can be long.\n\nMilestone: **M4** (operator, 2026-11-14; placement to decide). Source: operator UI review of 2026-11-14.\n\n### Context\n- The Messages list will no longer name the interlocutors of a group MP (« Interlocuteurs multiples » goes, #900); the list of participants can be long, so it does not belong in the row (operator, 2026-11-14).\n- The engine already knows how a group's members change (LOT-058: through the owner's reply, `newdest`; captures #336, #507). No screen shows the participants today (no « Participants » view in `App/SwiftHFR`).\n\n### To decide before coding (`status: needs-decision`)\n- Where: a toolbar entry of the group MP reader (« ⋯ » › Participants), a header above the first message, or a sheet.\n- The source of the list: what an MP page carries (to check against the captures of LOT-058; no HFR fact without a source, AGENTS.md §3.1).\n\n### Acceptance criteria (once decided)\n- [ ] In a group MP, the participants are reachable in one tap and listed; nothing changes in the Messages list.\n- [ ] One-to-one MPs unchanged.\n\nRelated: #858 (group MPs read like topics), #297 (LOT-171), LOT-058.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
